{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1242839-homebrew-imbue-item-hack","id":1242839,"title":"[Homebrew] Imbue Item Hack","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-04T19:00:09-07:00","id":1242839,"title":"[Homebrew] Imbue Item Hack","content":"The Enhanced and Imbued item merits and the Imbue item attainment are unfortunately vague and somewhat contradictory. I feel like this is because the Imbue item attainment creates items that fall under both the Enhanced item <i>and</i> Imbued item merits coupled with Enhanced items covering both a subset of items created with the Imbue attainment <i>and</i> those created by making a spell Indefinite or Lasting. What follows are rules for using the Imbue item <i>attainment</i> to create Imbued and Enhanced <i>items</i>.<br /> <br /> Dot values are determined for each spell separately before being combined for the final cost of the item; e.g. an item might contain a 3 dot spell and a 1 dot spell Imbued at 2 dots (for purposes of spell factors and reach), determine the effects of each separately before combining them into the final 5 dot item.<br /> Items created with the Imbue item attainment have Reach determined by the creator. These reach factors can be changed reflexively by the creator so long as they maintain spell control of the item; once the item is relinquished (safely or unsafely) reach can no longer be altered. Free reach is determined by the dot rating of the spell vs the dot rating it\u2019s Imbued at; a 1 dot spell Imbued as a 2 dot merit has two free reach, a three dot spell imbued at three dots has only one, and a five dot spell can only have more than one free reach if the item is created by an Archmaster. Reach above the safe limit does not add to the dot rating of the item, instead the item gets the Overreach X tag, where X is the number of unsafe reach effects applied.<br /> <br /> Imbued items (per the merit) created with Imbue item cast their spells with base primary factor equal to the merit dots assigned to the spell, as mentioned before reach is fixed by the creator and cannot be changed. The dicepool is Merit rating of the spell + Gnosis of the wielder, it requires a point of Mana to activate, and non-reach factors can be increased per the normal spellcasting dice penalties. Other supernatural creatures <i>do not</i> add their Supernatural Potency to the activation roll, these items are fueled by the Supernal and things like Primum or Blood Potency are meaningless. Paradox is rolled based on the wielder\u2019s Gnosis (0 for non-mages), and Overreach applies additional Paradox dice as if the extra reach was done by the wielder. Imbued items that do not have reach assigned to Instant casting use the wielder\u2019s Gnosis to determine ritual casting time.<br /> <br /> Enhanced items created with Imbue item are always-on effects that do not require mana to activate, instead they continuously affect the wearer, the item itself, or an area. The Duration of spells Imbued this way automatically become Indefinite and have their primary factor changed to Potency, this does not require reach or additional mana. Size and Area can be increased by one step for every two merit dots, similar to Legacy Attainments; Targets is not a relevant factor for Enhanced items. Clash of Wills is Merit + Supernatural Tolerance of wielder + 4 (due to Indefinite duration). Overreach add to the Paradox to be rolled whenever Quiessence would be caused and weekly (in addition to once a week rolls if the Imbuement itself wasn\u2019t safely relinquished); Paradox is rolled at the wielder\u2019s Gnosis.<br /> <br /> Examples:<br /> Ghostbuster Forge (Imbued Item ****)<br /> This Imbuement is placed some sort of container capable of holding weapons or ammunition. The weapons or ammunition is placed inside and then the Ghostbuster Forge is activated to place the <i>Ephemeral Enchantment </i>spell on all items inside. Reach is assigned to Advanced Duration and Advanced Scale; this item is designed to enchant large quantities of ammunition or several melee weapons at once for future threats, not to quickly enchant a single weapon for an emergency.<br /> <br /> Rhulak Math Nir\u2019s Bane (Enhanced Item ****)<br /> This spear was created for a Werewolf pack trying to deal with a magath known as Rhulak Math Nir; the pack had no luck determining Rhulak\u2019s <i>actual</i> bane and so commissioned this weapon to be created. Rhulak Math Nir\u2019s Bane has had the Ephemeral Enchantment spell woven into it with reach spent to act as the bane of Rhulak Math Nir.<br /> <br /> Ring of Mind Shielding (Enhanced Item **)<br /> A simple silver ring that imparts its wearer (of up to size 6) with the effects of the <i>Mental Shield</i> spell. Reach is assigned to Advanced Potency for an additional +1 bonus to Clash of Wills rolls. Clash of Wills is rolled with a dicepool of 7 + Supernatural Tolerance of the wearer. The ring does not magically resize itself, people with particularly thick or thin fingers may not be able to wear it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}